  "No work items match that filter at this stage.",
  "No, and it deliberately does not promise a number. It reports what it actually produced: sheets used, placed area, utilization per sheet and across the run, offcut and scrap, unplaced pieces, and how far the plan sits from an area-only lower bound. Any savings figure depends on your stock, your cutting list and your margins — not on a marketing claim.",
  "No. Basic covers a single user with inquiries and the proforma wizard. Business covers up to five users and the full document chain — sheet store, job orders, delivery notes, tax invoices, statements and reporting — without the cutting-optimization engine or the production-stage modules. Those two are the Factory tier.",
  "No. He is an estimator who taught himself what the work needed. That shows in the product: it is built around the workflow of a glass shop rather than around a software pattern, and it is deliberately plain to use.",
  "No. It is a Windows desktop application built with WPF on .NET 8. Your business data lives in SQLite database files in your own user profile on your own machine, and it works without an internet connection. There is no web dashboard, no tenant, and no online account to sign in to.",
  "No. It was written by one person who estimates glass for a living. There is no agency, no studio and no team behind it, and nothing on this site should read as though there were.",
  "No. Licensing is a single signed licence file activated offline, in five editions from Basic to Enterprise, with a 30-day full-feature trial. Nothing about sponsorship changes that: the model is a licence you own, not a subscription you rent.",
