  "ProGlass Automation",
  "ProGlass Automation brand banner showing the application's Overview dashboard with open inquiries, proformas raised, jobs in production and pieces ready to dispatch",
  "ProGlass Automation builds desktop software for glass fabrication businesses: estimation, calculation, cutting optimization, stock, production, delivery, invoicing and reporting.",
  "ProGlass Automation can load one complete demonstration workflow into an empty database. It is a single connected job — one enquiry, one quotation, one job order, one partial delivery, one tax invoice — with the same data flowing through every stage, and it refuses to run at all if the database already holds real records.",
  "ProGlass Automation contributors",
  "ProGlass Automation Demo",
  "ProGlass Automation developer",
  "ProGlass Automation editions",
  "ProGlass Automation editions — Trial, Basic, Business, Factory and Enterprise: which modules each tier unlocks, and how offline licensing works.",
  "ProGlass Automation has no company behind it. It was written by Juber Saleem, who estimates glass for a living and started building the software he needed because the paper version of the job kept costing him time. He is still estimating. How the application got to version 2.0.11 is written down, dated, and open to reading — and that record is a better description of its author than any biography.",
  "ProGlass Automation is a complete commercial chain with a cutting-optimization engine behind it, written and maintained by a single person. It is not short of ideas. It is short of hours, hardware to test against, and reviewed translations.",
  "ProGlass Automation is a Windows desktop application for glass fabrication. It holds the parts of the business that normally live in separate spreadsheets — the quotation, the glass build-up, the cutting plan, the stock, the deliveries and the invoices — and makes each one carry the last one forward.",
  "ProGlass Automation is built as one document chain carried by twenty-five view areas. This page walks the modules that make up the working day: what each one does, which screens it opens, and where in the product it sits.",
  "ProGlass Automation is built by one developer. What sponsorship funds, which work is open to collaborators, and how to get involved without buying influence.",
  "ProGlass Automation is desktop software for glass fabrication businesses: what it is, the problem it solves, how it is built and what it does not do.",
  "ProGlass Automation is desktop software. There is no cloud account, no subscription dashboard and nothing to sign in to on this website.",
  "ProGlass Automation is developed by {v1}. The developer page covers the build, the technology and the thinking behind it.",
  "ProGlass Automation is licensed per business with a signed licence file activated offline. The editions below are the ones the application itself defines, and the feature gating is the same map the navigation rail uses — so what this page says and what the application does cannot drift apart.",
  "ProGlass Automation is licensed with a signed licence file that is activated offline. There is no licence server that has to be reachable, and no account to create. This page describes what a customer needs to know.",
  "ProGlass Automation is Windows desktop software for glass fabrication businesses: estimation, SGU/DGU/lamination pricing, cutting optimization, sheet-store inventory, production stages, delivery, VAT invoicing and reporting.",
  "ProGlass Automation is written and maintained by one person. Sponsorship funds work — a cutting table to test export formats against, reviewed translations, test engineering — and never buys a roadmap position. The page below states the gaps as they actually are.",
  "ProGlass Automation is written by Juber Saleem, a glass estimator rather than a trained engineer. Its audits, fixes and open work are dated and public.",
  "ProGlass Automation is written by Juber Saleem, a glass estimator rather than a trained engineer. One person, no team, no investors — and how that shaped the product.",
  "ProGlass is a single-company system: one business, its own customers and its own staff. It is not built for multi-tenant hosting, and it does not want to be.",
  "ProGlass is sold to glass businesses with different shapes: a single estimator, a five-person office, or a factory running eight production stages. What you need ranges from the proforma wizard alone to the full chain plus the cutting-optimization engine. Quoting one number for all of those would mean either overcharging the first or underdelivering the last.",
