  "Raw stock arrives with edges that are not fit for a finished product, so a trim is cut off before any piece is placed. The trim is not the same for every glass: a thin pane can take 15 mm all round, a heavy pane may need 50 mm on three edges and none on the top. A layout that ignores this is optimistic by a few millimetres on every side — which is exactly enough to lose a piece.",
