  "Some optimizers place rectangles anywhere on the sheet. A glass table cannot work that way — it scores a line, breaks the sheet, and the piece comes free. So the engine models the cuts, not just the positions: it splits the remaining rectangle at each placement and records the split as a cut in the order the operator will make it.",
