  "Terms",
  "Terms covering this website and the use of the ProGlass Automation desktop application, including what the website does and does not claim about the product.",
  "Terms of use",
  "Test engineering",
  "Tests target the invariants that matter — company semantics, inquiry-to-quote conversion, price-basis determinism — and one of them scans the source tree for silently swallowed errors.",
  "TGI Spacer",
  "Thank you. Your request has been recorded and will be answered by email. If you would rather not wait, write",
  "That is the situation here. The application is real and in use on the commercial side: inquiry through statement, with the optimization engine and the eight production stages behind it. What it does not have is a second pair of hands, a test table to send cut files to, or a translation reviewed by somebody who works in the language.",
  "That page is not here.",
  "The 9-step wizard prices the job: company, client, project, pricing, the step-5 specification grid, charges, print preview, attachments, profit & loss.",
  "The account statement a customer accepts: filter, preview, pipeline, review.",
  "The account view a credit controller wants — customers ranked by value, by area or by pieces, with receivables and ageing attached to the same row. Sortable, searchable, exportable like every other report.",
  "The address you followed does not lead anywhere on this site. These are the routes people usually want.",
  "The animation below follows one worked example: a 3210 × 2250 plate of 6 mm glass, a 15 mm trim on all four edges, a 3 mm blade gap, and five pieces to come out of it.",
  "The answer arrives at month end, if it arrives, because cost was never captured against the job in the first place.",
  "The answers below are limited to what the application actually implements.",
  "The application can seed a single complete demonstration workflow into an empty database — one enquiry, one quotation, one job order, one partial delivery, one tax invoice. These are its numbers, read straight out of the seeder rather than chosen for a page.",
  "The application compares editions by order, not by name, so a stored licence keeps its meaning as new tiers are appended. The descriptions below are the definitions written on the edition enum itself.",
  "The application degrades to read-only rather than locking you away from your records, so you can still open and export your data. A licence that expires during a grace period behaves the same way. Reactivating restores write access.",
  "The application is a single WPF solution: views and view-models split one folder per business area, one database context per bounded context, and a design system the entire interface is drawn from. Localisation is resource dictionaries, so a new language does not need a code change.",
  "The application is a single WPF solution: views and view-models split one folder per business area, one database context per bounded context, and a design system the whole interface is built from. The same discipline shows in the numbers on this page — no debt markers in shipped code, policed by a test rather than by good intentions.",
  "The application is the argument. A demonstration will take you through the chain on a job you recognise.",
  "The application log and the audit trail — what it did, and who changed what.",
  "The application log and the audit trail, side by side.",
  "The application log and the audit trail: five severity levels, the last 500 entries kept in memory, error and warning counters, and the correlation ID that follows one operation across modules.",
  "The application log answers \"what did it do\" — startup, licence checks, seeding, production events, failures — and a log file is a diagnostic artefact. The audit trail answers \"who changed this, and when\", record by record, with the before and after of every field. Keeping them apart is why the log can be rolled and truncated without losing the record of who approved a quotation.",
  "The application seeds this job itself.",
  "The application ships four visual families and sixteen accent presets, all chosen from Settings. The card edge, the corner it turns on and the tint of the fill are set beside them. The same controls drive this website: press a plate below, or move the edge, and the page you are reading re-themes itself.",
  "The application ships the same idea in Settings → Appearance. For the full set — sixteen colour plates,",
  "The application stores documents, not summaries. A quotation becomes a job order becomes a delivery becomes an invoice — and each step keeps the audit record of the one before it.",
  "The application's Crystal Fluid family: see-through surfaces over a luminous environment.",
  "the application's default",
  "The application's Material-You family: surfaces derived from the accent's own dusk (its Golden Hour wallpaper).",
  "The application's own default — FontService.DefaultFontFamily.",
  "The application's strict default family — crisp sky over slate, minimal tinting.",
  "The approved proforma is what the job order is converted from.",
  "The assistant inside the application reads across the same records — stock, documents, activity, profitability, statements and analytics. It is deliberately read-heavy: there is exactly one write it can perform, and it is permission-gated, confirmed and audited.",
  "The awkward ones, answered first.",
  "The best screenshot is your own data.",
  "The blade gap consumed between cuts — 3 mm thin/medium, 4 mm thick",
  "The blog architecture is in place for regular writing: each note is a data entry with its own page, sitemap entry and metadata. New notes are added rather than retro-fitted.",
  "The border line on every card, the corner it turns on, and the padding that follows it.",
  "The build-up is worked out on a calculator or in a spreadsheet, and the basis it was priced on — glass, spacer, gas, labour — lives in that one file, if it is written down at all.",
  "The business chain",
  "The business, not a department.",
  "The chain",
  "The chain runs Inquiry ➜ Quote ➜ Confirm ➜ Produce ➜ Deliver ➜ Invoice ➜ Settle, and every document keeps its link to the one before it. That traceability is the point of the application.",
  "The client's LPO, the drawings and the approval scans, attached to the job and carried with it into the tax invoice and the statement.",
  "The colours and treatments, per pane",
  "The combined build-up: a laminated pane inside a double-glazed unit.",
  "The commercial chain — inquiry through statement — is complete in the application. The production stages are the current wave of work: eight shop-floor workstations and a control centre sitting under the same job order, so the office and the floor finally read from one record. After that the direction is depth rather than breadth.",
