  "The eight queues, and how much of each job is sitting in them.",
  "The eighteen section names are constants, and the file says why: grouping and filtering depend on them, and a free-typed name would quietly create a second \"Proforma Invoice\" that no filter would ever show. System Center then groups those sections into five scopes — all activity, transactions, inventory, system, users and security — over the same trail.",
  "The emergency option for a file too broken to open",
  "The engine",
  "The engine computes a deliberately weak lower bound on how many sheets the job needs using total area alone, then reports how many sheets the actual plan used above that bound. A gap of zero means no plan could use fewer plates. It is shown because 'how close was this?' deserves an answer rather than a boast.",
  "The engine exports generic DXF, Bottero .OPT, Intermac .ISO and Lisec .DAT. The formats are written to the published structures, but they have not been proven on every controller family.",
