  "The glass types you process",
  "The grid the job is priced in: one block per specification, GLASS TYPE · SPECIFICATION · BASE and SURCHARGE % on the block, and one row per glass line below it. Every panel bills at least 0.5 m², and a panel that reaches 4 m² takes the specification's surcharge rate.",
  "The grid's own action bar: QUICK makes the one fast pass Step 6 takes its sheet quantity from, OPTIMIZE searches the plans for fewest unplaced pieces then fewest sheets then highest utilisation, and VIEW RESULT opens the optimisation module on its summary.",
  "The guillotine nesting engine: eight tabs, two oracles, five machine export formats.",
  "The house margin profile, by thickness bucket.",
  "The idea",
  "The inquiry is recorded with its scope of supply. Converting it copies the BOQ rows onto the proforma's spec grid, where Step 4 prices each build group against the sheet costs you actually buy at. Step 5 then prices every panel — at least 0.5 m² of work each, base rate plus the specification's surcharge once a lite reaches 4 m² — and QUICK or OPTIMIZE hands Step 6 its sheet quantity.",
  "The interface",
  "The interface is drawn from one design system — tokens, not hard-coded colours — with four visual families and 16 accent presets. It has never been reviewed by an outside designer.",
  "The interface tour shows the screens a demonstration runs through, and the optimization page explains what the cutting engine does with a real cutting list.",
