  "The numbers are already there",
  "The one who wants the margin visible at the moment of quoting rather than at the end of the quarter.",
  "The one write is adjusting a sheet-stock quantity, which requires the SheetStore.Edit permission and a confirmation, and is recorded in the activity log. Over-issue is refused.",
  "The one-page order-to-cash funnel for anyone who does not want fourteen screens.",
  "The one-page order-to-cash funnel for the whole business.",
  "The only tier",
  "The optimiser writes Bottero .OPT, Intermac .ISO and Lisec .DAT. Those files deserve to be proved on a machine.",
  "The optimization engine",
  "The optimizer runs Auto or one of five stages, tries six plate patterns and six cut complexities, and two independent oracles check the plan before it is used. The result exports to CSV, Excel, DXF, Bottero .OPT, Intermac .ISO or Lisec .DAT.",
  "The other nine are above their reorder level, so only this one raises a flag — which is what a store report is for.",
  "The overall order report: a four-step wizard that reconciles the whole document chain.",
  "The overflow menu for secondary shell actions.",
  "The owner who prices the awkward jobs",
  "The pane and sheet source, then the charges the estimator adds: glass rate, tempering, holes, cut-outs, argon gas, silicon bed and wastage. Its figures stamp onto the specification in step 5, and the difference between the two is what the review step exists to show.",
  "The partial delivery",
  "The parts of the job this application holds.",
  "The per-proforma profit and loss the engine already computed, over a period.",
  "The period's VAT figures inside the reporting hub.",
  "The period's VAT figures, gathered from one calculator so they agree with the invoices.",
  "The person building it",
  "The piece list the run works from, including the outer/inner pane colours.",
  "The place the audit trail is read. Meaningful actions are recorded with their module, operation and context, so the question 'who changed this, and when' has an answer that is not a recollection.",
  "The plan",
  "The plates the engine is allowed to cut from, and what is left on each rack.",
  "The price basis is written down",
  "The price of a glass job is decided by four inputs: what the build-up is, how big the pieces are, what the glass cost, and what you want to make on it. ProGlass holds all four in one place.",
  "The problem",
  "The problem with a number",
  "The product has exactly one organising principle: a document is a conversion of the document before it, and every number on it keeps the context it was calculated with. Everything else — the wizard, the engine, the delivery chain — follows from that.",
  "The product is honest about what it does, but the in-repo documentation is written for engineers. A shop-floor user needs a task, a screen and a result — not a module map.",
  "The product's own vocabulary",
  "The Production Control Center assigns, starts, completes, holds and releases work, and records a reason when a job is blocked — so a stalled job has an explanation attached to it.",
  "The production-stage modules: Cutting · Holes & Cutouts · Polish · Edge Deletion · Mitring · Tempering · Pairing · Doubling / Lamination",
  "The profit figure is not recomputed from today's prices. It is the stored snapshot from Step 9 of the proforma, so a report opened next year still shows the margin the business actually quoted at, and a moved cost basis is visible rather than silently absorbed.",
  "The proforma is priced by specification group: clear tempered for the main facade, tinted where the sun hits, and a double-glazed Low-E unit for the energy-efficient zones. Each line carries its specification exactly as Step 5 holds it — serial, glass reference, outer pane W1 × H1, inner pane W2 × H2 where there is one, quantity, area, rate and value.",
  "The ProGlass Automation interface: dashboards, the proforma wizard, glass calculators, the optimization workspace, sheet store, delivery and reports.",
  "The ProGlass workflow stage by stage: inquiry, the 9-step proforma wizard, job order, production stages, multi-movement delivery, VAT invoices and statements.",
  "The project's history is written down, dated, and open to reading.",
  "The quotation",
  "The quotation, priced across three specification groups — 22 lines, 83 pieces, 160.79 m². Issued with a 30-day validity.",
  "The quote is not a document, it is a calculation",
  "The rack, as records: buy and use movements with history, never an edited number.",
  "The rate this row is charged at",
  "The rates in the seeded job are the sample dataset's own numbers. ProGlass Automation publishes no price list for glass, and nothing on this site is a market rate.",
  "The rates on the quotation are the sell prices of the sheets and consumables in the store. Stock levels, usage and reorder levels are live fields, not a report generated afterwards.",
