  "The seeded job is a demonstration. Yours would be your own.",
  "The sheet is not entirely usable",
  "The sheet price used at the moment of quoting is part of the quotation. When stock prices move next month, that quote should still show the margin it was built on, and the movement should be flagged rather than silently applied.",
  "The sheet store and the consumable inventory are seeded alongside the job, because a glass business is not only glass. Available quantity is stock minus used — the application's own live fields, not a derived figure.",
  "The sheet store keeps buy and use movements per sheet, so offcuts and remnants are stock the system knows about, and a sheet's history stays attached to it.",
  "The sheet-by-sheet schedule with its cuts in execution order.",
  "The single most important property of an ERP is that a number, once stored, stays what it was. ProGlass writes the calculation context next to the figure and reads it back.",
  "the site's own spacing",
  "The sixteen accents the application ships. Tap one and the whole site takes it.",
  "The software began as a way to stop retyping. It was not planned as a product, and there was no intention to sell it. It was one estimator removing the parts of his own day he kept getting wrong — and then discovering that the same day is happening in glass shops everywhere.",
  "The specification grid on step 5: # · glass ref · W1 H1 W2 H2 · qty · SQM · total SQM · rate · value, on a block carrying glass type, specification, base rate and SURCHARGE %",
  "The specification grid the quotation is priced from, and the profit-and-loss step that asks whether the price is good enough. Everything below is live: the grid prices as you type, and the profit-and-loss screen reads those same rows.",
  "The state",
  "The stock behind it",
  "The strategy family decides which placement portfolios get tried. Effort decides how hard the engine searches inside that family — time budget, shuffles and consolidation sweeps. Changing one does not silently change the other.",
  "The ten consumable items seeded into inventory.",
  "The thermal stage — and the routing rule that decides which panes ever reach it.",
  "The thermal stage, queued only for the treatments that require it.",
  "The thick bucket is deliberately asymmetric: thick glass takes no trim on the top edge. The minimum breakout is the narrowest offcut worth keeping — anything thinner is reported as trim waste rather than counted as reusable stock.",
  "The topic list is deliberately narrow. It follows the questions a glass business actually has to answer, not the keywords a software website usually chases.",
  "The total stock figure tells you how much glass you own. Consumption grouped by job tells you where it went, and that is the number that lets you price the next similar job with confidence.",
  "The trial",
  "The trial is issued automatically the first time the application runs.",
  "The vocabulary of a glass order",
  "The website's own palette — the application's Violet accent, taken deep.",
  "The whole application, grouped as its own rail groups it.",
  "The whole floor in one filterable table, whatever stage a piece is standing at.",
  "The widest shuffle set and MaxRects on every ordering. Expect minutes on a large job, not seconds — the app says so in its own hint text.",
  "Theme and colour",
  "Theme family, accents, mode, wallpaper, motion, per-module backgrounds",
  "There are 2,369 xUnit test methods across 288 files, and the workflow invariants — piece flow clamping, VAT tolerance, price-basis stamping — are the ones that must never regress.",
  "There is no cloud account, no tenant and no subscription dashboard. The application runs on one Windows PC, or on a handful that share a database file across the office.",
  "There is no CV here, because a CV is the part of a person you cannot check. What exists instead is six working documents at the root of the repository, each carrying the date it was written, describing what broke, what the evidence was, what changed and what is still open. Read together they are a working history of the software — and of its author — more specific than any biography.",
  "There is no office, no second developer, no designer, no translator and no one on support. The build is as far along as one estimator working evenings could take it. The next stage needs help, and the gaps are listed by name rather than hinted at.",
  "There is no price on this page, and that is deliberate.",
  "There is no sponsorship platform wired up yet, no tier list and no published amounts. Until there is, this is a conversation by email — which suits a product built this way.",
  "There is no subscription, no telemetry and no funding behind the project. Certificates, signing, the test hardware and the time spent on a release all come out of one person's pocket.",
  "There is no support tier between a customer and the author. Describe the job you do and where it goes wrong, and the answer comes back from the person who can change the software — usually with a question about how your shop actually works.",
  "These are not aspirations written on a wall. Each is enforced somewhere in the build, which is why they have survived at this size — and why a solo author can still answer for the result.",
  "These are the application's four families. Pressing one re-themes this page, which is exactly what it does to the application.",
  "These are the defaults the engineering assumes before an operator changes anything. Every value is editable per run, and 'Load house defaults' puts them back.",
  "These modules are explicitly listed as ungated, so a missing entry can never be mistaken for a deliberate free one. A test fails the build if a new module ships without somebody deciding either way.",
  "These six numbers come from the plate and piece sizes drawn above. They are not a benchmark, and the",
  "Thickness · COLOUR · TREATMENT · EDGE POLISH · PANEL EXTRA",
  "Thickness-aware margins, kerf and minimum breakout, LM/RM/TM/BM",
  "This is the face ProGlass Automation itself is set in.",
  "This is the same map the navigation rail consults. A module that is not in this table is open in every edition, and that is written down explicitly rather than left implied.",
  "This is the whole application in sequence. Each stage below names the statuses it stores, what it carries into the next stage, and the guarantee that keeps the handoff honest — because a chain is only as good as the weakest conversion.",
